    "ok": true,
    "error": null,
    "output": "(a) Root cause: Issues stay assigned to deliberately paused primaries with no live run. Recovery treats that as stranded work and keeps re-invoking. A deliberate pause (known resume) is not a first-class waiting path, so each sweep retries and gets \"Agent is not invokable (paused)\" \u2014 a churn loop, not a real strand.\n\n(b) One product rule: Deliberate assignee pause with a known resume is a live wait, not a strand. Until resumeAt (or a one-shot fallback handoff), do not re-invoke that assignee and exclude those issues from stranded recovery.\n\n(c) Invariants: (1) Other lanes/fallback keep productive work moving. (2) Only real failures escalate; intentional pause is not a blocker. (3) No infinite loop \u2014 one defer or handoff ends retries for that pause epoch.",
